{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>That our sons</b> — they are raised in their youth like saplings." "<b>Our daughters</b> — like a king's palace, for they are adorned and painted." "<b>Hewn</b> — like חטובות, after the manner of Egyptian work." "<b>The shape of a palace</b> — the sense is doubled."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 144, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:44.218538956Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}